# ClubOps Development Rules

- ClubOps is demo-first and live-ready.
- No real sensitive data in demo mode.
- All demo data must be fake.
- Do not hard-code data in UI components.
- Use provider interfaces for data.
- Keep modules modular and reusable.
- Keep UI simple for non-technical volunteers.
- Build mobile-responsive screens.
- Consider accessibility.
- Consider auditability.
- Consider security before feature convenience.
- Do not add paid APIs unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not leave lint, type or build errors.
- After each feature iteration, run lint, typecheck if available, tests if available, and build.
- Fix all errors before stopping.
- Update CHANGELOG.md, BUILD_NOTES.md and ROADMAP.md after every completed iteration.
- If Git is configured and authenticated, commit changes with a clear message.
- If a remote GitHub repository is configured, push after successful tests and commit.
- Never commit secrets, `.env` files, real personal data, or real club data.
